#![allow(clippy::excessive_precision)]
//! Golden-parity test for the tectonic-inversion pass (`PARITY_TESTING.md`)
//! — reference HTML lines 6641-6741, extracted by the Node harness described
//! in this port's `CHANGELOG.md` entry for heightmap import.
//!
//! Each case runs the real chain the reference runs — `buildReliefField` →
//! `pickPlateSeeds` → `classifyPlateCrust` → `reconstructBoundaryStress` →
//! `stampVolcanicArcs` — feeding each stage the previous stage's own
//! Rust output, so a failure names the first stage that broke rather than
//! only the last.
//!
//! `plate_id` is the one input handed in as a literal: the reference gets it
//! from `assignPlates()`, which has its own golden test
//! (`golden_parity_assign.rs`), so the harness computes an independent
//! brute-force Voronoi from the seeds instead. That keeps this test measuring
//! the inversion rather than re-measuring the Jump Flood.
//!
//! Assertions are exact (`assert_eq!` on `f32`), not tolerance-based: every
//! function here is deterministic integer/float arithmetic over the same
//! operation order, with `js_hypot`/`js_exp`/`js_round` covering the three
//! places V8's libm differs from Rust's. A tolerance would hide exactly the
//! bugs this is for.
//!
//! # Fixture shapes
//!
//! - `margin` / `margin_wrap`: a basin→shelf ramp with a narrow orogenic
//!   ridge and a rift trough — the geometry the pass is *about*. Between
//!   them they reach all six `BTYPE` codes and both crust signs, and the
//!   pair differs only in `wrap`, so the seam handling in
//!   `build_relief_field`/`reconstruct_boundary_stress` is isolated.
//! - `plateau`: elevations quantised to eighths, so many cells tie exactly.
//!   That reaches both tie-breaks — `pick_plate_seeds`' strict `<`
//!   (first wins) and `reconstruct_boundary_stress`' `>=` (last wins) —
//!   which continuous fixtures cannot.
//! - `flat_no_arcs`: entirely above sea level, so every plate is
//!   continental and `classify_boundary` can only return collision or rift.
//!   Pins `stamp_volcanic_arcs`' empty early return as *correct*, the
//!   branch the other three cases never take.

use cartalith_jsmath::js_exp;
use cartalith_terrain::infer::{
    build_relief_field, classify_plate_crust, pick_plate_seeds, reconstruct_boundary_stress,
    stamp_volcanic_arcs,
};

